# Generated count files. Every PR that adds/removes a file, test, or line edits
# these, so they collide on a three-way merge constantly (the O(n^2) "counter
# cascade"). Their content is fully derivable from the tree, so a textual merge
# conflict is never meaningful — the correct values are recomputed by
# scripts/docops/check_docops_integrity.py.
#
# These point at the `dharma-docops-counter` merge driver (keep-ours, no
# conflict). Register it once per clone with:
#     scripts/docops/install_docops_merge_driver.sh   (or: make onboard)
# After a merge, the live values are healed by:
#     python3 scripts/docops/check_docops_integrity.py --write-auto-sections --write-manifest-counts
# CI does both automatically (.github/workflows/docops-autorefresh.yml).
#
# NOTE: a custom merge driver only runs where it is registered (local clones +
# the autorefresh runner). GitHub's server-side merge ignores it, which is why
# the autorefresh workflow also re-syncs open PRs after main moves.
docs/docops/AUTO_INVENTORY.md merge=dharma-docops-counter
docs/governance/SOVEREIGN_MANIFEST.md merge=dharma-docops-counter
